    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0588" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d323-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent—priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-31">December 31, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>From the President for the Former Naval Person personal and secret No. 248.</p>
                <p>Arrangements for <hi rendition="#small-caps">Symbol</hi> satisfactory. Our Chiefs
                    of Staff will arrive twelfth and I will follow two days later so that we could
                    all meet together on fifteenth. I believe our staffs can cover the ground in a
                    two day preliminary conference. The prospect pleases me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d323-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d323-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
